      "fields_of_interest": "Multi-agent systems; co-design of systems; distributed optimization and control; applied topology and sheaf theory; applied category theory.",
      "research_program": "The program Riess has built at Georgia Tech since February 2025 rests on one mathematical premise: coordination in a networked system is a local-to-global problem, and sheaf theory is the branch of mathematics invented for exactly that problem. See [[ref:quantale-model]] and [[ref:convergence-theory]].\n\nA second line asks what happens when system properties are graded rather than binary; the same enrichment turns co-design feasibility into a quantitative trade-off.",
